    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented the threshold feature for `frai eval`. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n### Core Changes:\n\n**1. frai-core (`generateReport` function)**\n- Accepts optional `thresholds` parameter: `{ exact_match: 0.9, toxicity: 0.95 }`\n- Evaluates each threshold against metric scores\n- Adds `report.passed` (boolean) and `report.thresholds` (array) when thresholds provided\n- Each threshold entry: `{ metric, min, score, passed }`\n\n**2. CLI (`frai eval`)**\n- New `--threshold <metric=min>` option (can be used multiple times)\n- Example: `frai eval --outputs out.json --threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.95`\n- Validates thresholds before report generation\n- Exit codes:\n  - `0`: No thresholds or all thresholds pass\n  - `1`: One or more thresholds fail\n  - `2`: Malformed threshold or unknown metric (lists valid metric IDs)\n\n**3. Report Output**\n- **JSON**: Includes `passed` field and `thresholds` array\n- **Markdown**: Adds \"Thresholds\" section with PASS/FAIL status for each threshold\n\n**4. Tests**\n- Added comprehensive tests for:\n  - Passing thresholds\n  - Failing thresholds (score too low)\n  - Metrics with no score (fail their thresholds)\n  - No thresholds specified (backward compatible)\n\n**5. Documentation**\n- Updated README.md and frai-core README with threshold option docs\n- Added SDK example showing threshold usage with custom metrics\n\n### Key Behavior:\n- Without `--threshold`, behavior is unchanged (exit 0, no new fields in report)\n- Metrics with `score: null` always fail their thresholds\n- Works with custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations`\n- Invalid formats exit with code 2 and helpful error messages\n\nAll changes are backward compatible\u2014existing workflows continue to work as before.",
